.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
# Every .env variant, not just `.env` itself. A bare `.env` rule leaves `.env.cloud`,
# `.env.local-backup` and friends committable, which is exactly the file someone
# creates while switching between a local and a hosted database. `.env.example` is
# re-admitted below because it is deliberately tracked and holds no real values.
.env*
!.env.example
.pytest_cache/
.ruff_cache/
node_modules/
dist/
build/
*.egg-info/

# Frontend build artifacts (continuity/api/app.py serves web/dist/ once built) --
# already matched by the unanchored node_modules/ and dist/ patterns above; listed
# explicitly too so they are unmistakable.
web/node_modules/
web/dist/

# Generated data. ground_truth.json is regenerated deterministically from a seed and
# is deliberately kept out of the repo: the agent must never be able to read it.
data/*.json
data/*.parquet
data/*.csv
data/*.log
data/*.err
